(* fs-records-b2s C3, security result, (K_s, K_r, T_max) = (2, 3, 2): record
   replay rejection at the Server.  A Server peer never accepts the same
   sequence twice in one session, whoever registered it and whatever the
   plaintexts.  The direction is fixed to Beacon-to-Server, whose
   FsReceived events only the Server receive emits; the Beacon's finish is
   the definitional check C3-finish (fs-records-b2s-c3-finish.pv).  Also
   the target of the controls C-RETAIN and C-STALE. *)
query s: bitstring, b: bitstring, kid: key_id, root: bitstring, t: nat,
      m1: bitstring, m2: bitstring, i: time, j: time;
  event(FsReceived(beacon_to_server(), s, b, kid, root, t, m1))@i
  && event(FsReceived(beacon_to_server(), s, b, kid, root, t, m2))@j
  ==> i = j.

process FsRecordsB2sMain()
